#: ../../electronic/bond_order.rst:249
msgid ""
"RKS-PBEの値は、パラメータを含まない一様TB模型の値と小数点以下2〜3桁まで一致し、 中央8本の平均は0.637で :eq:`bo-"
"uniform` の :math:`2/\\pi` に等しい。したがって、 RKS-"
"PBEで見える交替は有限鎖の端による効果として理解でき、:math:`N` とともに 小さくなる。一方、RHFの交替振幅は :math:`N` "
"を増やしてもほとんど変わらず、 端の効果では説明できない結合の強弱、すなわち結合次数波（BOW）が鎖の中央に 残っている（:ref"
":`peierls-bond-order-wave` を参照）。"
msgstr ""
"The RKS-PBE values agree with those of the parameter-free uniform TB "
"model to 2–3 decimal places. The mean over the eight central bonds is "
"0.637, equal to the value in Equation :eq:`bo-uniform`, :math:`2/\\pi`. "
"The alternation in RKS-PBE can therefore be understood as an effect of "
"the ends of the finite chain and decreases as :math:`N` increases. In "
"RHF, however, the alternation amplitude hardly changes as :math:`N` "
"increases. The alternating strong and weak bonds that persist at the "
"center cannot be explained by end effects and constitute a bond-order "
"wave (BOW) (see :ref:`bond-order waves in a chain with fixed atoms "
"<peierls-bond-order-wave>`)."

#: ../../electronic/bond_order.rst:256
msgid ""
"スピン非制限計算（:math:`N=32`）では、スピン和の密度行列から求めた :math:`B_i` は ほぼ一様になり、UHFで0.312"
"、UKS-PBEで0.531と、スピン制限計算の平均値より小さい。 α電子とβ電子が1つおきの原子に分かれて局在すると、隣接原子間で同じスピンの "
"電子を共有する程度が下がり、スピン和の密度行列の非対角要素も小さくなる。"
msgstr ""
"In spin-unrestricted calculations (:math:`N=32`), :math:`B_i` from the "
"spin-summed density matrix becomes nearly uniform, at 0.312 for UHF and "
"0.531 for UKS-PBE, both below the mean values from spin-restricted "
"calculations. When α and β electrons localize on alternating atoms, "
"neighboring atoms share fewer electrons of the same spin, and the off-"
"diagonal elements of the spin-summed density matrix decrease."

#: ../../electronic/bond_order.rst:262
msgid "解釈と限界"
msgstr "Interpretation and Limitations"

#: ../../electronic/bond_order.rst:264
msgid ""
"結合次数は観測量ではなく、定義と基底関数に依存する指標である。結合エネルギーや 結合の長さとは異なる量であり、相関はあっても一対一には対応しない。"
" :eq:`bo-energy` のようなエネルギーとの関係は、電子間相互作用のない模型で成り立つ "
"ものであり、自己無撞着な平均場計算や相関のある計算では、そのままの形では成り立たない。"
msgstr ""
"Bond order is not an observable but a measure whose value depends on the "
"definition and the basis functions. It is distinct from bond energy and "
"bond length. It may correlate with those quantities, but there is no one-"
"to-one correspondence. A relation to the energy such as Equation :eq:`bo-"
"energy` holds for models without electron–electron interactions, but it "
"does not apply in the same form to self-consistent mean-field or "
"correlated calculations."

#: ../../electronic/bond_order.rst:269
msgid "非直交基底での結合次数は、直交化や分割の方法によって値が変わる。1原子に多くの 基底関数がある場合や、広がった基底関数を使う場合は特に注意する。"
msgstr ""
"In a nonorthogonal basis, bond orders depend on the method of "
"orthogonalization or partitioning. Take particular care when there are "
"many basis functions per atom or when the basis includes diffuse "
"functions."

